# The Guide — THE LOCALISED VARIANT of guide_fight_film.keys. Identical
# except for the last beat, which presses 8 at the cluster victory to
# toggle the word list into English.
#
# WHY THERE ARE TWO. The ENGLISH edition's victory footer reads "press any
# key to continue" — there is nothing to toggle to, so 8 would simply leave
# the screen. Every localised edition, pure German or mixed alike, offers
# the toggle and therefore has a second victory screen. Odiin, 2026-09-20:
# "the last scene is the second victory screen if there is one, or the first
# one if that's the only one". Verified on the German pure edition before
# this file existed: 8 turned Feuerball into Fireball rather than exiting.
#
# The Guide — STORE set, route D: the boss fight (slot 3) and its victory (slot 4)
# for cluster 1.1, in the locale's PURE edition. Same kit as route A.
# LAUNCH WITH FLASHBOSS_KIT_FIGHT_READY=1 in the environment: the forge then stamps
# the kit's cluster mastered-but-unfought (showcase_mode.stamp_fight_ready), which is
# what makes Know Your Enemy offer the fight; the cards are not due, so this route
# never enters the review.
LOG The Guide — store set, route D (the fight)

{LANG_KEYS}
KEY ENTER
EXPECT Core
KEY 1
# the session menu ("BEGINNING SESSION FOR CORE": 5 sanctum · 6 review mode · 7 path ·
# 8 tier-skip challenge) → 5 the sanctum → 4 KNOW YOUR ENEMY → 1 the cluster (a digit
# picks it on the tier page) → 5 fight on the confirm screen. The REGULAR fight:
# position 1 on battle_order[0], the order sorted by interval — which the forge's
# fight-ready stamp fixed (kit card 1 at 34 opens, kit card 8 at 13 closes). NEVER
# 8 on the session menu: that is the BossRun, a sandbox fight with a shuffled order
# (it asked Mimic in the danger zone on 2026-09-16).
KEY 5
KEY 4
KEY 1
KEY 5
# NO key at the "Engaging Boss" splash: a timed hold that reads nothing.

# ── slot 3: the FIRST battle frame — hero on rung 1, boss on rung 2, the opening line

# ── FILM: every beat of The Guide's fight, for the site GIF ───────────────
# Same walk as the store route; the three stills become a frame per beat. The
# Guide is a PARALLEL pack, so its boss asks a category question in the
# interface language rather than the immersion English of the Roots packs —
# which is the point of filming it separately (boss_fight._english_question).
EXPECT [1-8]\.
EXPECT ₃    ₄
REFUTE ₁    ₂
EXPECT {CARD1}
EXPECT ▓+\s*\Z
SHOT frame01
ANSWER
SHOT frame02
ANSWER
SHOT frame03
ANSWER
SHOT frame04
# The setback. MISS is a bench verb (key_script.py, resolve_miss; landed on
# shoot-automation at 39a2a3d2 with tests). Its comment there carries the
# reason in Odiin's own words, so this file does not repeat it.
MISS
SHOT frame05
ANSWER
SHOT frame06
ANSWER
SHOT frame07
ANSWER
SHOT frame08
KEY ENTER
EXPECT {CARD1}
EXPECT 🎆\s*\Z
SHOT frame09
# the word list, toggled into English
KEY 8
SHOT frame10
LOG film route taken
END
